## 2. Pipeline flow (sheet order = data flow)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    CD[ControlDetails\ncontrol metadata]

    subgraph SRC_SIDE[Source side]
        IF[InputFiles\nwhere/how to read SRC files]
        FM[FieldMappings\nSRC raw field -> SRC_ field]
    end

    subgraph TGT_SIDE[Target / regulator report side]
        IFT[InputFiles_TGT\nwhere/how to read TGT files]
        FMT[FieldMappings_TGT\nTGT raw field -> TGT_ field]
    end

    EN[Enrichments\nlookup/reference joins onto SRC]
    ENT[Enrichments_TGT\nlookup/reference joins onto TGT]
    ENTFPR[EnrichmentsTGT_FinalPostRec\npost-recon enrichments, e.g. NACK/valuation status]

    ELIG[Eligibility\n_CTRL rules: is this trade in scope?]
    OBLIG[Obligation\n_CTRL rules: who must report it?]
    REC[RecRules\nSRC vs TGT pairing + reconciliation status]
    BE[BreakExplain\n_CTRL_EXP rules: classify/explain the break]

    CD --> IF --> FM --> EN
    CD --> IFT --> FMT --> ENT
    ENT --> ENTFPR
    EN --> ELIG
    ENT --> ELIG
    ELIG --> OBLIG
    OBLIG --> REC
    ENTFPR --> REC
    REC --> BE
```

**Sheet tab order in the workbook** (left to right, matches the flow above):
`ControlDetails → InputFiles → FieldMappings → Enrichments → InputFiles_TGT → FieldMappings_TGT → Enrichments_TGT → EnrichmentsTGT_FinalPostRec → Eligibility → Obligation → RecRules → BreakExplain`

