## 4. Naming convention (apply consistently in any new config)

| Suffix | Meaning | Applied on |
|---|---|---|
| `_SRC` | Field sourced from / derived on the **source** (internal trade system) side | FieldMappings, Enrichments |
| `_TGT` | Field sourced from / derived on the **target** (regulator report) side | FieldMappings_TGT, Enrichments_TGT |
| `_CTRL` | A boolean/derived **control flag** produced by a rule (Eligibility, Obligation, RecRules) | Eligibility, Obligation, RecRules |
| `_CTRL_EXP` | A boolean/derived flag specifically for **break-explain** classification | BreakExplain |
| `_INFO` (mid-name, e.g. `PAYMENT_DATE_INFO_SRC`) | Raw/unprocessed intermediate field kept for reference before final transform | FieldMappings |
| No suffix (`StandardField`) | A field considered common/normalized across SRC and TGT, populated by coalescing `_SRC`/`_TGT` | RecRules |

Raw incoming column names (left, `FieldName`) are typically **UPPER_SNAKE_CASE** (SRC/legacy system export) or **PascalCase / friendly names** (TGT/regulator report), while internal normalized names (`NewFieldName`) are always **PascalCase + `_SRC`/`_TGT` suffix**.

