## 6. Sheet-by-sheet schema

### 6.1 `ControlDetails`
Two columns only: `FieldName` | `FieldValue`. One row per metadata item.

| FieldName | Example value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Regulation | CFTC-P45 | Regulation/rule identifier |
| ControlName | Trade-State-Comp | Human control name |
| ControlType | TRADESTATE | Enum: e.g. TRADESTATE, VALUATION, etc. |
| SubControlName | (blank) | Optional sub-control |
| AssetClass | CO | Short asset class code |
| AssetClassLongName | Commodities | Full asset class name |
| ControlDescription | free text | Template: "This is the {Regulation} Population Completeness Control for {Entity} {AssetClassLongName} to {Target}." |
| BusinessDate | T-2 | Offset convention used throughout the control |
| Frequency | DAILY | DAILY / WEEKLY / etc. |

### 6.2 `InputFiles` (SRC) and `InputFiles_TGT` (TGT — same schema)
One row per source dataset/file pattern (a control can read from multiple source systems).

| Column | Meaning | Example |
|---|---|---|
| DataSetName | Logical name of the source system/dataset | Apollo, Murex, DTCC |
| Environments | Comma list of environments the pattern applies in | DEV,UAT,PRE-PROD,PROD |
| FileDirectory | Path, using `{{^RootFileDir^}}` token for the environment root | `{{^RootFileDir^}}\Source Data\Incoming Data\Apollo COMM` |
| FileNamePattern | Regex to match the file, capturing the date/variable segment in `(.*)` | `APOLLO_COM_POS_STATE_HBEU_(.*)(.prn)$` |
| FileType | prn / csv / gz / dat | prn |
| FileDelimiter | Delimiter char if flat/delimited | `;` |
| FileSource | Source system short code | APOLLO |
| FileRegion | Region/booking hub code | HBEU, HBUS |
| ExcelSheetName | If FileType is xlsx, which tab to read | (blank unless xlsx) |
| FileDateSelection | Date offset convention for picking the file | T-2 |
| FileNameDateFormat | strftime pattern matching date embedded in filename | %Y%m%d |
| StripTopRowsCount | Header/junk rows to skip at top | 3 |
| StripBottomRowsCount | Junk rows to strip at bottom / notes | free text allowed, e.g. "File arrives 5.30pm the next day" |

Each distinct file/region/system combination = its own row. `FileNamePattern` always ends `(.*)(.<ext>)$`.

### 6.3 `FieldMappings` (SRC) and `FieldMappings_TGT` (TGT — same schema)

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Action | `AddColumn` (new derived field) or `RenameColumn` |
| DataSetName | Must match a DataSetName from InputFiles/InputFiles_TGT |
| FieldName | Raw incoming column name |
| NewFieldName | Normalized internal name, `_SRC`/`_TGT` suffixed |
| RegFieldNumber | Optional link to regulator's numbered field spec |
| TransformFunction | See §7 decision tree |
| TransformInputs | Comma-separated field(s)/literal(s) the function consumes, in order |
| TransformedFromValueOrFormulaInputTypes | Type of each input, same order as TransformInputs |
| (rightmost) Formula/value text | Free-text expression when TransformFunction = Formula |

### 6.4 `Enrichments` (SRC) and `Enrichments_TGT` (TGT — same schema)

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| EnrichmentName | Logical name for the lookup |
| LookupKeyFields | Join key field(s) on the main record |
| StaticFileNamePattern | Regex for the reference file (comma-separated fallback patterns allowed) |
| FileDelimiter | Delimiter of the static file |
| FieldNames | Column(s) read from the static file |
| NewFieldNames | Name(s) given to the joined-in field(s) |

Standard reference files seen: party mapping, intragroup mapping, country/region mapping, exception/response-code extracts, LEI/legal-jurisdiction reference. **Reuse these across controls where the same static file genuinely applies — don't recreate a lookup that already exists.**

`EnrichmentsTGT_FinalPostRec` = same schema, but for enrichments that can only be resolved after an initial SRC/TGT pairing pass (e.g. NACK/valuation status).

### 6.5 `Eligibility`
`Action | RuleNumber | FieldName | NewFieldName | RuleDescription | RuleFunction | RuleInputs | RuleFromValueOrFormulaInputTypes | RuleToValueOrFormula`

RuleNumber: `{RegulationShortCode}-Eligibilty-NN`.

**Boilerplate (reuse unchanged):** internal-trade checks (LEI-based and counterparty-based), CMACNYK exclusion, physically-settled exclusion, different-TR exclusion, US-person/affiliate check, live-trade check, expired-trade check, matured/terminated check, and the `IndepEligibility_CTRL` rollup pattern (AND-combination of the above).

**Asset-class-specific (must define fresh):** reportable-product rule(s) per source entity, spot/short-dated-forward exclusion thresholds, any commodity/FX-style edge case (e.g. precious-metals-as-commodity-not-FX).

### 6.6 `Obligation`
Same column shape as Eligibility. RuleNumber: `{RegulationShortCode}-{Entity}Obligation-NN`.

**Boilerplate:** entity-in-scope check (jurisdiction match), house-vs-counterparty reporting-party logic based on counterparty type + buy/sell.

**Asset/source-system-specific:** booking-system prime-brokerage (PB/give-up) logic — review per new source system; final obligation rollup with `UNKNOWN` fallback when any input is unresolved.

### 6.7 `RecRules`
Same column shape. RuleNumber: `RecRules-NN`.

**Boilerplate (reuse unchanged):** `ReconciliationSide` (PAIRED/SRC/TGT based on pair-key status), `IndepEligibilityObligation` (combine Eligibility+Obligation, gated by ReconciliationSide), `TRSObligation` (select the right party's obligation), `TRSVsIndepEligibilityObligation` (concatenated status string), `ReconciliationStatus` (final break/pair classification).

**Generated per-config (not boilerplate, but mechanical — see §3):** the `StandardField` coalesce block — one row per field that exists on both SRC and TGT, always `Formula`, pattern `{Field}_SRC if IsNotNull({Field}_SRC) else {Field}_TGT`.

### 6.8 `BreakExplain`
Same column shape, `_CTRL_EXP` suffixed outputs. RuleNumber: `BreakExplainRule_NN`.

**Boilerplate:** matured check, NACK check.

**Asset-class/source-system-specific (must define with SME):** stale/blank valuation scenarios (SEF vs non-SEF), under/over-reporting patterns specific to a source system, orphan-position scenarios, any control-vs-report disagreement scenario unique to that asset class's booking behavior.

