## 7. TransformFunction / RuleFunction — decision tree

Use this to pick a function instead of pattern-matching from memory:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Q1{Does the value\nchange per row?} -->|No, constant\nfor the whole control| SetValue
    Q1 -->|Yes| Q2{Is it copied from\none input field,\nunchanged?}
    Q2 -->|Yes| CopyField
    Q2 -->|No| Q3{Is it two+ fields\njoined into a string?}
    Q3 -->|Yes| Concatenate
    Q3 -->|No| Q4{Is it a date field\nneeding reformatting?}
    Q4 -->|Yes| ConvertDateFormat
    Q4 -->|No| Q5{Is it a day-count\nbetween two dates?}
    Q5 -->|Yes| CalculateBusinessDays
    Q5 -->|No| Q6{Is it a code/enum\nlooked up in a fixed\nreference table?}
    Q6 -->|Yes, must always resolve| MapValues
    Q6 -->|Yes, ok to be blank\nif no match| MapValuesDefaultNull
    Q6 -->|No| Formula["Formula\n(general conditional/\nboolean/string logic)"]
```

**Function reference:**

| Function | Use |
|---|---|
| `SetValue` | Hardcode a constant/context value onto every row |
| `CopyField` | Copy one field's value into a new field name unchanged |
| `Formula` | General conditional/boolean/string expression |
| `MapValues` | Look up a value in a fixed mapping table |
| `MapValuesDefaultNull` | Same, but defaults to null if no match |
| `Concatenate` | Join two or more fields/literals into one string |
| `ConvertDateFormat` | Reformat a date field from one strftime pattern to another |
| `CalculateBusinessDays` | Compute business-day count between two dates + a weekday/holiday list |

**Formula syntax (provisional — confirm against real file):** conditions appear to follow `"<value>" if <condition> else "<value>"` chains (Python-conditional-expression-like), with `IsNotNull(field)` as a null check, string literals in double quotes, and `in (...)` for set membership. Field references use the exact `NewFieldName` from earlier sheets, not raw column names. **Do not invent new operators or syntax beyond this pattern without flagging it as new.**

`RuleInputs`/`TransformInputs` and their `...ValueOrFormulaInputTypes` column must stay **positionally aligned** — input #3 in one list is the type of input #3 in the other.

