## 8. Negative examples — what NOT to generate

| Wrong | Why | Right |
|---|---|---|
| `TradeDate` (no suffix) in FieldMappings | Loses SRC/TGT distinction, breaks RecRules coalescing | `TradeDate_SRC` or `TradeDate_TGT` |
| `IsEligible` (no `_CTRL`) in Eligibility | Not distinguishable from a raw data field | `IsEligible_CTRL` |
| `RuleInputs = A,B,C` with `...InputTypes = str,int` (length mismatch) | Breaks positional alignment the engine relies on | Every input must have exactly one matching type entry |
| Inventing a new reportable-product rule without asking | Silently encodes a compliance judgment nobody approved | Draft it, label `NEEDS SME REVIEW`, ask |
| A brand-new TransformFunction name not in §7's table | Engine won't recognize it | Use §7's decision tree; flag explicitly if none fit |
| Skipping the `StandardField` coalesce for a field that exists on both SRC and TGT | Field will appear twice / inconsistently downstream | Always coalesce SRC/TGT pairs in RecRules |
| Reusing an Enrichments lookup file for a different join key without checking | Silent data-quality bug | Confirm the lookup key still applies before reusing |

